# Git Workflow

After making code or content changes in this repository:

1. Commit the relevant changes with a clear message (unless the user explicitly says not to commit).
2. Push to the remote branch immediately after committing — do not leave changes only on disk or only committed locally.
3. Confirm commit hash and push success in the response.

Do not push unrelated untracked files (e.g. `.DS_Store`, local `memory/` notes) unless the user asks to include them.
